    {
      "author": "Raegan Lavant",
      "date": "2026-06-30",
      "rating": 5,
      "source": "Google",
      "text": "I wanted to recognize Mr. John Forney for the great job he does. Every time I see him around the property, he’s always friendly, approachable, and willing to help. He’s very responsive whenever a maintenance issue comes up and always takes the time to make sure residents are taken care of. His positive attitude and professionalism don’t go unnoticed, and it’s clear he genuinely cares about the community. We really appreciate everything he does!",
      "responded": true,
      "response": "Raegan, thanks for your kind words about John! We're so glad to hear that his friendliness and responsiveness have made such a positive impact on your experience. We appreciate your support and are glad to have you in our community.\nBest, Erika Kelly, Property Manager",
      "responseDate": "2026-07-14"
    },
    {
      "author": "Kimberly Thorbourne",
      "date": "2026-06-18",
      "rating": 1,
      "source": "Google",
      "text": "Update 6/18/26: I pretty certain I won’t be renewing my lease. Nothing has improved since new management came in unfortunately.\n\n1 out two of our elevators has NOT WORKED since February 2026. No one in the office can tell us when it will be fixed.\n\nThe parking garage doors haven’t worked properly since March 2026\n\nThe hallways always smell! Very strong pungent smell. Never smells clean and very rare that it does. The floors are cleaned once a week. One day there was a lot of blood on the first floor by the elevator and it stayed there Friday night thru Mon morning when cleaning staff came back.\n\nThe roaches have gotten worse!! Luckily I am very clean so don’t see them a lot in my unit but definitely more than. Did when I first moved in 3 years ago. The pest control even came and insisted I remove EVERYTHING from all of my cabinets, just to not even spray in them (my surveillance camera is proof).\n\nNot to mention, the one thing we could count on is our pool opening Memorial Day weekend..! It’s June 18 and it’s still not open and they have no date on when it’s opening. My loft faces the pool and I have to look out my windows and see a pool that is DISGUSTINGLY and looks like it is filled with pee!!\n\nWe pay for luxury and convenience and are offered a shitshow!! LITERALLY!!\n\nIt sucks because my LOFT is AMAZING!!\n\n————————\nI loved it when I first moved here but the conditions and cleanliness of the common areas has gone completely downhill! If I wasn’t so in love with my loft, I would move. Even my mother who was visiting noticed the difference. The 5th floor goes DAYS without being cleaned… the same stains on the floor and trash lay there for days at a time.\n\nOh and the elevators NEVER work. I can’t tell you how many times I have been stuck on the elevator or had to carry groceries from the parking garage to the 5th floor!! Lmao off at LUXURY.",
      "responded": true,
      "response": "We appreciate your feedback, Kimberly. We understand your concerns about cleanliness and the elevator's functionality. It's important to us that we maintain our common areas to the best of our ability. We'd value the chance to discuss your experience further. Please feel free to reach out.\nPlease contact us at 404-842-1301 or eonmanager@castlegateprop.com",
      "responseDate": "2026-06-19"
    },
    {
