      "author": "Kathy",
      "date": "2026-01-19",
      "rating": 1,
      "source": "Google",
      "text": "I tour properties for my clients and read reviews to make sure all standards are met. During my recent visit, the tour was brief, but cleanliness is definitely something to pay attention to.\nAfter reading reviews, I’m concerned about situations where big corporate management companies may take advantage of hardworking tenants. To anyone reading this, here are steps you can take to protect your rights in Georgia:\nDocument any issues – Take photos or videos of safety hazards, maintenance problems, or unsanitary conditions.\nNotify management in writing – Clearly explain the issues and request timely fixes.\nContact local code enforcement – Report unsafe conditions, sanitation concerns, or building code violations to your city or county authorities.\nSeek legal guidance – Organizations like Georgia Legal Aid can help you understand your options.\nPut rent in escrow through the courts – If the landlord fails to address serious habitability issues, Georgia tenants may have the right to deposit rent with the court while repairs are made.\nKnow your rights under Georgia law – Landlords must maintain rental properties in livable, safe conditions.\nTake action to ensure your home is safe, clean, and properly maintained — don’t let anyone take advantage of you!",
      "responded": true,
      "response": "Thanks for your visit and for taking the time to share your thoughts, Kathy. It's crucial for us to hear about your experiences as we strive to improve our community. We understand your concerns and assure you that our residents' well-being is a priority. We’d appreciate the chance to address your concerns directly. Please reach out to us at your convenience.\nPlease contact me at 404-842-1301 or eonmanager@castlegateprop.com",
      "responseDate": "2026-01-19"
    },
    {
      "author": "Abrar Shaik",
      "date": "2026-01-19",
      "rating": 1,
      "source": "Google",
      "text": "Worst decision you’ll ever make !!!\nA big NO to this place. You will find cockroaches in every single corner. If you request for maintenance they will take a long time though after a long time the issue will not be resolved. They will use your floor mats without your permission and throw them on floor they don’t even care about it. No security. Once in every week you can find elevator problems, parking gate problems.\nThe Management especially people be sitting in leasing office rude and will give you so much attitude. After all this someone from the property will reply blah blah blah, but they don’t accept these things. I can throw out a lot pictures here but I’ve realised that is waste of time.If you ever made a decision to move in you gonna regret through out your lease! Advice: don’t believe in room tour they show. Just reply to this i can actually show you the real side if this place",
      "responded": true,
      "response": "We appreciate your feedback. Your experience is crucial to us, and we take your concerns seriously. We understand that you've experienced issues with maintenance and our team's conduct. We strive to create a welcoming environment and are dedicated to improving. We'd value the chance to discuss your experience in greater detail. Please feel free to reach out to us.\nPlease contact me at 404-842-1301 or eonmanager@castlegateprop.com",
      "responseDate": "2026-01-19"
    },
