      "rating": 1,
      "source": "Google",
      "text": "Overall: 2/5\nUnits: 4/5\nLocation: 3/5\nCleanliness: 0/5\nAmenities: 1/5\nOther Residents: 2/5\nManagement/Leasing: 1/5\n\nThe only redeeming qualities about this discount apartment complex are the units look nice and it’s next to a MARTA. I had arguably the best unit layout with the best views of the city and still won’t hesitate to leave after my lease ends.\n-Cleanliness - this complex is infested with bugs, there was a german roach infestation at one point. We kept our apartment pretty clean and our traps still catch 1-2 bugs a day.\n-Amenities: One or both elevators break down weekly. Elevators sound clunky and the buttons/electronics didn't work in them so you can’t tell which floor you are on. One time the elevators were down so I had to take the stairwell and there was a homeless person sleeping in it, this is apparently a reoccurring problem. Garage gates are left wide open for long periods exposing our cars. Gym is below average, equipment is all old and damaged. I wouldn’t go near pool since so many bugs in this complex. In-unit appliances are average. Maintenance doesn’t show up unless you call them.\n-Residents: a significant number of residents in the complex live in filth and are the reason there’s so many bugs. Some throw trash directly in the stairwells or in the elevators or leave their trash outside their door during non-valet days, or on the floor.\n-Management/Leasing: Leasing will get defensive with you or speak to you in a smarta** way if you raise an issue with them, nobody taught them customer service. Leasing wouldn’t show us where our unit was located or any pictures until move-in day. Management doesn't communicate anything to the residents and isn’t strict on cleanliness. They apologized once because both elevators were down for an entire weekend.\nTo summarize this apartment complex is incredibly below average and poorly managed. Don’t make your decision off the first floor that they show you, as others have mentioned.",
      "responded": true,
      "response": "Thank you for your feedback, Shahed. We're disheartened to hear that you've had a disappointing experience. We acknowledge your concerns about cleanliness and pest control, as well as the issues with amenities and our team's service. We take these matters seriously and would like to have a personalized discussion to see how we can improve. Please reach out to us directly. Your input is vital, and we're committed to enhancing our community for all residents.\nPlease contact me at 404-842-1301 or eonmanager@castlegateprop.com",
      "responseDate": "2025-10-19"
    },
    {
      "author": "nooria hashemi",
      "date": "2025-10-19",
      "rating": 1,
      "source": "Google",
      "text": "WARNING: Do NOT move here!\n\nThis place is a nightmare. The building is infested with German cockroaches — they crawl through the halls and into your apartment no matter how much you clean. Management has even sent out emails admitting the infestation, so they know it’s bad. I am terminating my lease early after 6 months of trying to make it work here.\n\nMaintenance is useless and takes forever. Our shower and dishwasher were broken, and when our AC went out during Atlanta’s summer, our apartment hit 85°F. The elevator is constantly broken and feels unsafe. The parking gate is always broken too, so there’s no real security.\n\nThe halls reek and are dirty — except for floor 1, which looks nice because that’s the only floor they show you during tours to trick people into moving in.\n\nThey lied during the tour, saying Fetch wasn’t used, but it absolutely is. Many residents are being evicted, and the complex is NOT dog friendly at all.\n\nThe only positives: it’s next to a MARTA station and the apartment layouts are decent — but that’s where the good ends.\n\nSave yourself the stress. This place will destroy your peace of mind. DO. NOT. MOVE. HERE.",
      "responded": true,
      "response": "We're truly sorry to hear about your experience, Nooria. Acknowledging your concerns about cleanliness and maintenance, we assure you that we're committed to enhancing our community. We understand your frustration and want to assure you that your satisfaction is a priority for us. We invite you to contact us directly for a more personalized discussion on this matter. Your input is valuable and we're eager to improve.\nPlease contact me at 404-842-1301 or eonmanager@castlegateprop.com",
      "responseDate": "2025-10-19"
    },
