    {
      "author": "Douly L",
      "date": "2025-09-19",
      "rating": 2,
      "source": "Google",
      "text": "Do not waste $2,000 a month on this place—it is absolutely not worth it.\n\nThe elevators almost never work, which means I’m constantly having to carry my child up several floors. One of the biggest problems is the roaches. They are everywhere, and no matter how clean you try to keep your apartment, it feels like the issue never gets resolved. It makes the living conditions uncomfortable and unsanitary, and management does not take it seriously.\n\nThe air conditioning at the elevator entrance doesn’t work, and the units there are filthy and dirty, which makes those areas even more unpleasant to be in—especially when the elevators already barely work.\n\nThe cameras don’t appear to work, which makes the place feel unsafe. My headphones were even stolen in the gym, and nothing could be done about it. The garage gates are almost always broken, forcing me to drive around to the other entrance, which is usually stuck open—making the property feel even less safe.\n\nIt feels like management only puts effort into the lobby and entertainment center instead of addressing the real problems residents face. The poor maintenance, lack of security, and overall neglect make it feel like you’re paying luxury prices for low-quality living.\n\nThe apartment layout itself is nice, but that’s about the only positive thing I can say. Everything else needs major improvement.",
      "responded": true,
      "response": "Thank you for sharing your feedback, Douly. We regret to hear that your experience at ibex at Uptown hasn't met your expectations. Your concerns about maintenance and cleanliness are important to us and we want to ensure they're addressed. We're committed to enhancing the living experience for all residents and would appreciate the opportunity to discuss your concerns further. Please contact me at 404-842-1301 or eonmanager@castlegateprop.com",
      "responseDate": "2025-09-19"
    },
    {
