    {
      "author": "t pope",
      "date": "2025-09-19",
      "rating": 1,
      "source": "Google",
      "text": "So i moved here after the huge fire on Cheshire. The apartment itself is nice but the roach infestation is INSANE. i have MAJOR concerns regarding safety, shortly after moving in the apartment there was a homicide in the parking garage, yet safety seems to be the least of the staffs concerns. The gates to the garage are broken and left up more than they are closed. The security doors from the stairwell leading to the outside have been broken/unlocked for MONTHS leading to homeless ppl sleeping in the stairwell on the regular. It’s super scary. The maintenance men are some of the rudest people I’ve ever encountered..it’s  to the point I don’t want them in my apartment. The broken doors and garage gates lead to my packages being stolen and homeless people constantly camped out in the stairwell. The hallways and elevators are disgusting. Dirty floors/elevators are usually left filthy for days if not weeks. The pool has been closed most of the summer and the grills have never worked since I’ve been here. The office staff aren’t terrible but if they are not out making rounds on the property what good is being nice if complaints and concerns about safety and cleanliness fall on deaf ears.",
      "responded": true,
      "response": "We're grateful for your feedback. Hearing about your experience is important to us and we take your concerns seriously. We recognize your mention of pest control and maintenance issues, as well as your worries regarding the gates and doors. We're dedicated to enhancing our community and we encourage you to reach out for a more personalized discussion. We're here to listen. Please contact me at 404-842-1301 or eonmanager@castlegateprop.com",
      "responseDate": "2025-09-19"
    },
    {
      "author": "manner plus",
      "date": "2025-09-19",
      "rating": 1,
      "source": "Google",
      "text": "Avoid This Roach-Infested Hellhole – You’ll Regret Moving In!\n\nOh man, this apartment is a total revolting nightmare that makes you wanna puke just walking in. Roaches are crawling absolutley everywhere: the hallways are teeming with them, scurrying like they own the place, and don’t even get me started on behind the kitchen appliances greasy hordes hiding back there, and they dart out from the fridge seals like a biblical plague every time you open it. It’s so filthy,\n\nI couldn’t even keep food without feeling sick. The air constantly reeks of this overpowering greasy beef fry smell mixed with pungent weed that seeps through the walls and vents, choking you out and clinging to your clothes and furniture like some nasty vomit you can’t wash off. Headaches all the time from that toxic combo.\n\nAnd the swimming pool? Perpetually closed for “maintenance” that’s never happening – it’s just sitting there as a slimy, mosquito-breeding joke they promised during the tour. The leasing office is the worst part; they’re heartless liars who couldn’t care less about tenants, acting like nothing’s wrong while your complaints go ignored.\n\nJoy and Pam are the slimiest of the bunch, insisting on all communication via email only so they can dodge any direct talks, and they twist everything around when it’s clearly their fault like botching repairs or paperwork and then gaslighting you. Lived here for months feeling trapped in a dumpster fire of neglect and disgust. Save yourself the pain and run far away you’ll gag just remembering it!",
      "responded": true,
      "response": "We appreciate you taking the time to share your experience at ibex at Uptown. We're sorry to hear that your experience hasn't been as expected. Your feedback regarding pests, aromas, and the pool is important to us. Our team is here to listen and discuss your concerns in more detail. We're dedicated to enhancing our community, your satisfaction is our priority. Please contact us at 404-842-1301 or eonmanager@castlegateprop.com",
      "responseDate": "2025-09-19"
    },
